Show initial content in one transaction / defer_initial_window_show

This change applies to zed-industries/zed 90d8514059561f0e44af0a32e84e1c329cef3232
after patches/0001, 0002, 0003 and 0004.

What it does:
- defer_initial_window_show(): opt in during the app callback before the
  first window. Untabbed normal windows stay hidden until the callback
  returns, then order and request the first frame in one CATransaction.
- Hidden/popup/tabbed-window behavior is unchanged.
- Display link starts on the next main-queue turn.
- Drop sets closed so deferred show cannot touch a dying window.

Do not turn presents_with_transaction back off
after the initial transaction (patches/0002 keeps it on for every frame).

Three-way on bcf6582: one conflict in MacWindow::drop. Upstream #64143
drops the accesskit adapter to break the window-close retain cycle; the
patch stores closed so deferred show cannot touch a dying window. Keep
both: closed.store first, then accesskit_adapter.take.

Applied cleanly onto 90d8514 after 0001–0004. #65170's redraw-before-reveal
stays in activate(): a hidden window gets setNeedsDisplay before
makeKeyAndOrderFront. While initial_show_pending, displayLayer still
returns without drawing, so that setNeedsDisplay does not present early;
show_initial_windows still orders and requests the first frame in one
CATransaction. #65059's display_changed_callback is untouched. The
initial transaction's request-frame callback stays
RequestFrameOptions::default() (no display-link signal yet).

Re-apply on a roll: git apply --3way patches/0005-defer-initial-window-show.patch
